WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:06.960
Speaker 1: Former New Jersey Governor Chris
Christie, former Trump endorser Chris Christie

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:12.940
is going to be running against Donald Trump
and the other Republicans in the primary field

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.150
for the Republican presidential nomination.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:22.869
NBC News is now reporting former New Jersey
Governor Chris Christie to announce his 2024

00:00:22.869 --> 00:00:24.820
presidential bid on Tuesday.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:29.099
It is Christie's second run for the nomination.

00:00:29.099 --> 00:00:32.860
He will announce at a town hall in Manchester,
New Hampshire.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.370
Two sources were confirmed.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:40.690
The article reminds us that Chris Christie
stumbled is the word they used to a sixth

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:44.320
place finish in 2016 as New Hampshire primary.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.110
Axios was the first to report the timing of
Christie's announcement after he dropped out

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.510
of the race eight years ago.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:57.660
Christie endorsed Trump days before Super
Tuesday, lending a credible name to Trump's

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.420
momentum.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:04.600
Another interesting aspect to this is that
ABC News is immediately suspending its relationship

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:05.600
with Chris Christie.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.790
Chris Christie has been a analysts contributor
sort of person on ABC.

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:15.430
ABC has announced that at least for now, they
are suspending their relationship with Chris

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:19.260
Christie because he is indeed becoming an
official candidate.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.920
So I'm going to be very transparent with everybody
here.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:29.380
If you came to me maybe with tears in your
eyes and said, David, if you knew that one

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:34.490
of the Republicans currently running would
be the next president of the United States,

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:35.820
who would you pick?

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.520
I pick Chris Christie.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:43.290
And when you say to me, okay, well, there's
Trump, there's DeSantis, Nikki Haley, Tim

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.180
Scott and Mike Pence.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:48.970
Vivek Ramaswamy At this point, I don't even
remember who else is running.

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:51.400
You've got, I guess.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.600
Asa Hutchinson, God forbid.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.799
No, listen, I mean, from this group I go with
Chris Christie.

00:01:57.799 --> 00:02:03.149
Chris Christie as a New Jersey governor, a
blue state that sometimes elects Republican

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:07.479
governors in the mode of what we've seen happen
in Massachusetts as well over the years.

00:02:07.479 --> 00:02:10.599
William Weld, Mitt Romney.

00:02:10.599 --> 00:02:15.200
I can't believe I'm blanking a Charlie Baker
more recently.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.150
I would I would be if you said forget about
Democrats.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.270
It's just it's going to be one of these Republicans.

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:21.590
I think I go with Christie.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:25.150
I actually think Christie is more intelligent
than a lot of the other people he's running

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:26.150
against.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:30.360
I will remind folks that this could be a factor
if Christie gets on the debate stage with

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.510
Trump.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.200
Christie is actually pretty good in debates.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:41.750
And remember these moments back from 2016
when Christie really made Marco Rubio look

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:46.120
stupid by pointing out that Rubio is in a
sort of talking point coma, repeating the

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.420
same thing over and over and over again.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:49.420
Remember this classic moment?

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.030
Speaker 3: You have not been involved in a
consequential decision where you had to be

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:54.030
held accountable.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:57.740
You just simply haven't seen what the people
at home to think about this.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.010
That's what Washington, D.C. does.

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:05.140
The drive by shot at the beginning with incorrect
and incomplete information, and then the memorized

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:07.200
25 second speech.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.310
That is exactly what he's.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:10.640
Unidentified: See.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:11.959
See, Marco.

00:03:11.959 --> 00:03:12.959
Marco.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.260
The thing is this.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:20.660
Speaker 3: When you're president, United States,
when you're a governor of a state, the memorized

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:24.470
32nd speech where you talk about how great
America is at the end of it doesn't solve

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.879
one problem for one person.

00:03:25.879 --> 00:03:29.299
Speaker 2: This notion that Barack Obama doesn't
know what he's doing is just not there.

00:03:29.299 --> 00:03:30.299
It is.

00:03:30.299 --> 00:03:31.299
He knows exactly what.

00:03:31.299 --> 00:03:32.630
Speaker 3: The memorized 25 second speech.

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:37.090
Speaker 2: That's there in the campaign.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:38.810
Speaker 3: You know what she means?

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:39.810
Get into this.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:40.810
You know what the shame is, Marco?

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:41.810
The shame is that you would actually criticize
somebody for showing up to work, plowing the

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:46.220
streets, getting the trains run back on time
when you've never been responsible for that

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.220
in your own life.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.220
Speaker 1: All right.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.700
So listen, Chris Christie can debate.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:56.390
I would be from an entertainment standpoint,
I would be very interested in seeing the approach

00:03:56.390 --> 00:04:01.170
that Christie would take to Trump from a pragmatic
standpoint.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:05.771
If I had to pick from this group of Republicans,
who is the next president, it would be Chris

00:04:05.771 --> 00:04:06.771
Christie.

00:04:06.771 --> 00:04:08.880
And I think probably by a long shot.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:13.459
It is, I think, maybe interesting or important
to note.

00:04:13.459 --> 00:04:17.829
There are MAGA people already making fun of
Chris Christie for being obese.

00:04:17.829 --> 00:04:18.829
Trump's obese.

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:25.010
It's stunning to me that the supporters of
one obese candidate are making fun of another

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:27.070
candidate for also being obese.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:29.490
I mean, yes, Christie seems more obese than
Trump.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:35.389
I saw some tweets going around about Chris
Christie doesn't need to run for president.

00:04:35.389 --> 00:04:36.900
He just needs to run.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.160
Like, go out and jog in order to lose weight.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:45.440
If that's the best that the MAGA people can
come up with against Christie, I actually

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:50.830
am very interested to see whether Chris Christie
can get some traction because he is quick,

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:56.880
he's got a quicker wit, he's smarter, he has
experience as a prosecutor, a sort of experience

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:02.660
that is lacking and in the Republican primary
and might actually be interesting if confronted

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.060
with Trump on a debate stage.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:06.480
So I'm going to be following the Chris Christie
candidacy.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:07.889
Interesting closely.

00:05:07.889 --> 00:05:12.530
And from an interested perspective, if it's
Christie versus Biden, I'm voting for Biden.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:15.540
Certainly, I agree with Biden much more on
policy.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:16.990
But I think that that's the most interesting.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.830
You know, Vivek Ramaswamy so boring.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:21.479
Tim Scott dead on arrival.

00:05:21.479 --> 00:05:22.479
Who cares?

00:05:22.479 --> 00:05:23.479
Pence Oh, my goodness.

00:05:23.479 --> 00:05:27.220
Pence might try to bore the audience into
submission, but Chris Christie, I find a little

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.220
bit interesting.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.490
Let me know your thoughts.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:34.650
Make sure you're subscribed on YouTube at
YouTube.com, slash the David Pacman Show.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:36.469
We'll take a quick break and be right back

